>> title: Brioche
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, french, butter, eggs, enriched
>> counters: Bakery
>> pairs-with: lemon-curd
>> servings: 12
>> time: 15 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — the butter goes in a piece at a time and the dough has to stay cool: one that warms while it beats splits into grease and butter and will not come back

>> step: whisk the dry mix
Whisk @bread flour{2 1/2%cup}(340 g), @granulated sugar{3%Tbs}(40 g), @instant yeast{2%tsp}(6 g), and @table salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g) together.

>> step: beat in 5 min
Beat @eggs{4%large}(200 g) and @whole milk{1/4%cup}(60 mL) into @&(~1)dry mix{} for ~{5%min}.

>> step: beat in a piece at a time, 10 min
Add @softened unsalted butter{3/4%cup}(170 g) to @&(~1)dough{} in pieces, beating ~{10%min} until glossy.

>> step: cover, chill overnight
Cover @&(~1)dough{} and chill ~{12%hours}.

>> step: shape a log, proof in a 9x5-in loaf pan
Shape @&(~1)dough{} into a log and proof in a #9x5-in loaf pan{} for ~{2%hours}.

>> step: brush, bake 350°F 35 min
Brush @&(~1)loaf{} with @beaten egg{1%large} and bake at 350°F for ~{35%min}.
